('performance','HI','HI - Heat Insulation','Work shoes designed to protect the foot from heat transmitted by conduction. The entire footwear is tested on a surface at 150 °C, verifying that the increase in internal temperature does not exceed the required standards. They guarantee effective thermal insulation in environments such as foundries, steel mills, industrial plants and road construction sites where work is performed on hot surfaces.',NULL,5),
('performance','HRO','HRO – Heat-resistant sole for contact','Soles that are resistant to heat contact. The test involves contact with a hot surface of 300°C for 60 seconds without visible damages.',NULL,6),
('performance','LG','LG - Ladder grip system','Safety shoes designed with a specific sole profile for a secure grip on ladder rungs, reducing the risk of slipping during ascent and descent. Indicated for electricians, installers, construction workers and anyone who frequently works at heights on fixed or portable ladders.',NULL,7),
('performance','PL','PL - Perforation-resistant shoe (4.5 mm nail)','Safety shoes according to EN ISO 20345:2022 equipped with a non-metallic perforation-resistant insert, tested with a large diameter nail (4.5 mm). This requirement guarantees effective protection of work shoes against the penetration of sharp objects through the sole, with the advantage of an insert that is lighter and more flexible than traditional metal inserts.',NULL,8),
('performance','SC','SC - Scuff cap abrasion resistance','Safety shoes equipped with a toe cap with high resistance to abrasion, tested with 8,000 Martindale cycles. The Martindale test evaluates the durability of the material in the toe area, ensuring that the work shoe maintains its protective features over time even in the most wearing working conditions.',NULL,9),
('performance','SEAMLESS UP','Seamless Upper','Footwear featuring a seamless upper that ensures greater comfort, lightness, and reduced irritation even during long working days.',NULL,10),
('performance','SR','SR - Slip resistance','Safety shoes equipped with a sole with advanced anti-slip performance, specifically designed to ensure maximum stability and grip even on the most insidious surfaces. Subjected to severe dynamic friction tests under wet and lubricated conditions, this footwear ensures a firm grip on the ground and drastically reduces the risk of accidental falls. It is the ideal solution to guarantee maximum safety on wet or oily floors, typical of critical environments such as professional kitchens, laboratories and food processing plants.',NULL,11),
('performance','WR','WR - Waterproof shoe','Safety shoes totally waterproof thanks to upper, seams and joints tested to prevent the entry of liquids. The waterproofness of the entire shoe is tested by placing it in a water tank and subjecting it to a dynamic flexion or mechanical walking test.',NULL,12),
('performance','WRU','WRU - Water-resistant upper','Work shoes with water-resistant upper thanks to a specific special treatment. The laboratory test involves the mechanical flexion of the material in contact with water for 60 minutes, verifying that the passage of water inside is practically zero.',NULL,13),
('performance','LIGHT','Light','The combination of a composite toecap (Light Cap) and a synthetic anti-perforation insole (High Flex) allows for a lighter, more comfortable safety shoe that causes less fatigue for the operator.',NULL,14),
('performance','METAL FREE','Metal Free','This shoe is totally designed without metal parts.',NULL,15),
('performance','FLEX','Flex','The combination of a puncture-resistant composite insole (High Flex), an EVA midsole, and a rubber outsole creates an extremely flexible shoe. A flexible shoe is more comfortable and less tiring for the wearer''s foot.',NULL,16),
('performance','P','P - Perforation-resistant shoe','Safety shoes equipped with a METALLIC perforation-resistant insert placed in the sole. The test involves resisting penetration by a standardized nail with a diameter of 4.5 mm applied with a fixed force of 1100 N: the insert must resist without being perforated, guaranteeing maximum protection against sharp or cutting objects that may be stepped on during work activities. The difference between P and PL is the fact that the PL''s perforation-resistant insert is not made of metal, but P''s is.',NULL,17),
